1
00:01:54,719 --> 00:01:55,620
Congratulations! Congratulations!

2
00:01:55,659 --> 00:01:56,939
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

3
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,340
Everyone, eat and drink your fill!

4
00:01:58,379 --> 00:01:59,900
This ceremony was long overdue.

5
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:00,439
Sit, sit, sit.

6
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:01,540
Go grab some chairs.

7
00:02:01,599 --> 00:02:02,120
Go get the chairs.

8
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:03,019
They're here, they're here!

9
00:02:05,519 --> 00:02:07,379
Aunt, you made it!

10
00:02:07,879 --> 00:02:08,439
Wonderful!

11
00:02:08,439 --> 00:02:09,620
What an honor to have you here.

12
00:02:11,219 --> 00:02:12,139
Fanhu didn't come?

13
00:02:12,259 --> 00:02:13,159
Fanhu, he...

14
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,020
he's picky.

15
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:16,840
And his stomach's bad.

16
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,979
Afraid your big feast

17
00:02:19,379 --> 00:02:20,539
would upset his stomach.

18
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:22,439
Qi Deyao.

19
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:24,960
You didn't get his share of the money,

20
00:02:25,259 --> 00:02:26,960
yet you prepared such a lavish feast.

21
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,039
Doesn't that mean

22
00:02:28,479 --> 00:02:29,159
you took a huge loss?

23
00:02:29,439 --> 00:02:30,300
It's only right, it's only right.

24
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,580
No profit to make, but I've still got my pride.

25
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,500
Look, this belated one-month banquet,

26
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:35,960
what a grand affair it is!

27
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:37,979
Thanks, thanks for the compliment.

28
00:02:40,599 --> 00:02:41,360
My precious granddaughter,

29
00:02:41,419 --> 00:02:41,960
can Grandpa hold you?

30
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:42,860
Did she spit up her milk?

31
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:44,240
She spit up.

32
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:45,960
See, she spit up.

33
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:47,419
She spit up, she spit up.

34
00:02:48,199 --> 00:02:49,060
Pat her back, pat her back.

35
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:49,639
Is she okay?

36
00:02:50,819 --> 00:02:51,280
Real smooth.

37
00:02:52,099 --> 00:02:52,460
Xiaofang.

38
00:02:52,479 --> 00:02:52,879
That's lovely.

39
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:56,699
Uncle.

40
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:58,639
Since you're being so sincere,

41
00:02:58,699 --> 00:03:00,000
our family should make a gesture too.

42
00:03:00,599 --> 00:03:01,180
Right, Grandma.

43
00:03:01,599 --> 00:03:02,840
Bit's one-month banquet

44
00:03:02,879 --> 00:03:03,599
is being held at our place.

45
00:03:03,759 --> 00:03:04,560
Once you drink this cup of tea,

46
00:03:04,639 --> 00:03:05,900
we'll bury the hatchet.

47
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:07,819
Aunt.

48
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:09,180
My sincerity,

49
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:10,039
you've all seen it.

50
00:03:11,319 --> 00:03:12,319
The past between us,

51
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,400
let's just turn the page on it.

52
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:14,599
Bit, after all,

53
00:03:14,659 --> 00:03:16,139
carries the blood of both our families.

54
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,180
Since Fanhu isn't here,

55
00:03:18,319 --> 00:03:18,879
this cup of tea,

56
00:03:19,099 --> 00:03:20,039
I'll offer to you, elder.

57
00:03:20,939 --> 00:03:21,300
Fine.

58
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,319
For Bit's sake,

59
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:25,840
I'll give you face.

60
00:03:26,439 --> 00:03:27,120
Thank you, Aunt.

61
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:28,759
Good.

62
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:33,460
Good.

63
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:34,879
Good.

64
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:36,240
Let's stop standing around.

65
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:37,900
Take your seats, let's eat!

66
00:03:38,039 --> 00:03:38,840
Come, take your seats, take your seats.

67
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,340
My dad said

68
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,379
you volunteered to host

69
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,379
the one-month banquet.

70
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:45,259
Did he force you into it?

71
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:47,080
Listen, you absolutely can't cave in.

72
00:03:47,099 --> 00:03:47,620
You hear me?

73
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,379
I'm not caving in.

74
00:03:50,139 --> 00:03:51,360
Your dad stole Bit's hair

75
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,139
to register her household.

76
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:53,300
And then he put on that fake crying act.

77
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:54,939
This time...

78
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,020
This time what?

79
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,639
I'll play hardball.

80
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,199
Wait, Dad, what's wrong with your face?

81
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:08,800
Why does my face feel numb?

82
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:10,560
Only my face feels numb.

83
00:04:11,479 --> 00:04:12,000
Wait, I...

84
00:04:12,979 --> 00:04:14,539
Uncle, what's wrong with your face?

85
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:15,800
Yeah, what's wrong with my face?

86
00:04:15,919 --> 00:04:17,240
Don't tell me it's a stroke!

87
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:18,319
No...

88
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:19,300
Sit down quick, sit down first.

89
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,379
Come on, sit down first.

90
00:04:20,439 --> 00:04:20,980
Sit down first.

91
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:21,540
Sit, sit, sit.

92
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:22,800
I can't speak clearly.

93
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:24,459
Oh my gosh, it really is a stroke!

94
00:04:25,019 --> 00:04:26,220
Auntie, quick, go get a blanket!

95
00:04:26,279 --> 00:04:27,279
Get a blanket, okay okay okay.

96
00:04:27,839 --> 00:04:28,860
No, no, no.

97
00:04:29,339 --> 00:04:30,180
Coming, coming!

98
00:04:31,139 --> 00:04:31,899
Here's the blanket.

99
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:33,279
No...

100
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,279
No, I, I, I...

101
00:04:35,279 --> 00:04:35,819
Deyao.

102
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:37,420
You mustn't catch a chill again!

103
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,360
He's just mumbling.

104
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:39,240
What's he saying?

105
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:40,220
He's saying...

106
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,819
why is Xiaowei holding tape?

107
00:04:44,579 --> 00:04:45,279
This tape...

108
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,560
Of course, it was prepared for you in advance.

109
00:04:55,939 --> 00:04:56,959
Old Bit.

110
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,220
He doesn't want to watch.

111
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:07,959
Hurry, hurry.

112
00:05:08,339 --> 00:05:09,459
Everyone's here now.

113
00:05:10,019 --> 00:05:11,639
Why aren't those two dishes cooked yet?

114
00:05:11,699 --> 00:05:12,639
Mom, Mom.

115
00:05:12,639 --> 00:05:13,240
Hurry up!

116
00:05:13,279 --> 00:05:13,680
Don't worry about it.

117
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,779
Go eat, dinner's ready.

118
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,339
There are still two dishes uncooked.

119
00:05:16,439 --> 00:05:17,360
Don't worry, you all go eat.

120
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,019
Come on, let's go eat.

121
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,000
Go sit down.

122
00:05:20,399 --> 00:05:21,540
You all go ahead and eat.

123
00:05:21,579 --> 00:05:22,759
There are still two more dishes.

124
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:24,439
Auntie, don't trouble yourself.

125
00:05:24,439 --> 00:05:25,100
This is plenty.

126
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:25,720
Sit down quick.

127
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:26,180
Right.

128
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:26,560
Sit.

129
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:27,379
This...

130
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:30,920
I...

131
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,100
I can't sit here, I...

132
00:05:33,519 --> 00:05:33,819
Mom.

133
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,220
This is exactly where you should sit.

134
00:05:35,279 --> 00:05:36,019
Sit down, sit, sit, sit.

135
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:36,860
Right, Mom.

136
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:38,100
You should sit here.

137
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,439
You're the head of this family.

138
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:40,199
If it weren't for you,

139
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:41,480
I'd have run off with my son long ago.

140
00:05:42,399 --> 00:05:43,819
Qiumei, sit, sit.

141
00:05:53,779 --> 00:05:54,759
Half my life I've been a doormat.

142
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,199
From now on, for Bit,

143
00:05:58,959 --> 00:05:59,699
for the child,

144
00:06:01,339 --> 00:06:02,839
as his grandma, I've got to

145
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:04,759
step up.

146
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,600
Come on, let's have a toast.

147
00:06:13,939 --> 00:06:14,959
Everyone, dig in!

148
00:06:15,399 --> 00:06:16,459
Okay, okay okay okay.

149
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:22,220
Little baby.

150
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:23,339
Bit.

151
00:06:24,339 --> 00:06:25,079
Look at him.

152
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,160
So adorable.

153
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,860
Makes me want to have another one.

154
00:06:29,319 --> 00:06:29,939
You go have one.

155
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:30,579
Exactly.

156
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:37,300
Don't worry.

157
00:06:38,399 --> 00:06:40,220
I just put some herbs in your teacup.

158
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:41,379
Your mouth's just numb.

159
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:42,199
It's not a stroke.

160
00:06:43,139 --> 00:06:44,220
The effect will wear off soon.

161
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:47,079
Dad.

162
00:06:47,639 --> 00:06:48,959
How does it feel to be tied up?

163
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:50,920
Do you know why my brother and I

164
00:06:50,959 --> 00:06:52,319
both refuse to come home?

165
00:06:53,779 --> 00:06:54,680
Growing up,

166
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:56,000
it felt like we were always

167
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:56,639
tied down by you like this.

168
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,339
As a kid I didn't like fatty meat,

169
00:07:03,459 --> 00:07:05,360
so you had Mom cook it every single day,

170
00:07:05,379 --> 00:07:06,079
forcing me to eat it.

171
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:07,720
Saying it was good for me.

172
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:13,279
These are all the things you don't like.

173
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:15,519
You're getting old,

174
00:07:16,019 --> 00:07:17,220
so you really need to watch your health.

175
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:18,420
Eat.

176
00:07:44,019 --> 00:07:44,740
Glad you made it.

177
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:46,180
Haiyun, look after the guests.

178
00:07:46,399 --> 00:07:46,740
Dad.

179
00:07:48,079 --> 00:07:49,339
Do you remember when I was little,

180
00:07:49,339 --> 00:07:50,600
how much I loved to draw?

181
00:07:53,899 --> 00:07:55,839
I remember one Father's Day,

182
00:07:57,079 --> 00:07:58,720
I drew a picture for you.

183
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:01,680
It took me a whole week.

184
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,480
I thought back then,

185
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:07,899
you'd praise me after seeing it.

186
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,220
But you didn't even look at it.

187
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:12,000
Right in front of me,

188
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:12,980
you tore it up.

189
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:17,759
Said drawing was a waste of time.

190
00:08:18,779 --> 00:08:20,040
Then all of my drawings,

191
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:20,699
you tore them all up.

192
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,420
And snapped my pencils, too.

193
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:24,420
Lucky for me, Mom was kind.

194
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:26,000
She felt sorry for me.

195
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,740
She saved me a box of paints,

196
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:29,740
and a brush too.

197
00:08:30,399 --> 00:08:31,759
But you still found them in the end.

198
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:32,759
And threw them all out.

199
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:38,519
Later I moved out.

200
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:40,539
No one was there to control me.

201
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:44,600
So I wanted to start drawing again.

202
00:08:46,419 --> 00:08:48,200
But when I picked up the brush,

203
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,220
I couldn't draw anymore.

204
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:02,179
All those ideas of mine,

205
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:04,399
the images I wanted to create,

206
00:09:05,559 --> 00:09:06,059
they were all gone.

207
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:10,779
Why do you think that is?

208
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,340
Bound too long, thanks to you.

209
00:09:35,059 --> 00:09:35,500
Dad

210
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:40,200
I tied you up this one time

211
00:09:41,679 --> 00:09:43,620
so now we're even, you and me

212
00:09:54,419 --> 00:09:55,120
I'm a dad now

213
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,100
So stop meddling in my life from now on

214
00:09:58,580 --> 00:09:59,279
And what's more

215
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:02,500
I won't let Bit end up like me

216
00:10:03,779 --> 00:10:04,519
And I definitely won't

217
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,019
treat Bit the way

218
00:10:06,019 --> 00:10:06,820
you treated me

219
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,200
Sure, of course we do!

220
00:10:19,039 --> 00:10:20,139
Xiaofang did such a great job

221
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,399
Come on, drink up

222
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,379
A boy or a girl, it's all the same

223
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:57,879
Look here.

224
00:11:05,980 --> 00:11:06,700
Sis.

225
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:07,879
Let's put it somewhere else.

226
00:11:08,799 --> 00:11:09,919
Last time you hid it there and forgot.

227
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,139
Before we even left the house,

228
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,240
Mom had already found it.

229
00:11:12,419 --> 00:11:13,259
Look at my memory.

230
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:14,539
How about we put it right here?

231
00:11:14,539 --> 00:11:15,840
Stop hiding it.

232
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:18,200
Mom.

233
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:20,539
This old lady's doing just fine.

234
00:11:20,799 --> 00:11:22,779
I don't want money from any of you.

235
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:24,860
Just come home.

236
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,779
That's better than anything.

237
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:28,159
Mom, take it, take it.

238
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:28,919
Take it.

239
00:11:28,919 --> 00:11:30,559
Look, brimming with a mother's love.

240
00:11:31,259 --> 00:11:31,919
So much stuff.

241
00:11:32,039 --> 00:11:33,960
These are all things you two love to eat.

242
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,700
Divide it up yourselves in Shenzhen.

243
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:37,460
Mom...

244
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,720
Mom's two precious treasures.

245
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,399
Grandma.

246
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,200
Is there Spiced Pressed Duck that I love?

247
00:11:45,379 --> 00:11:46,240
Of course.

248
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,600
How could Grandma ever forget you?

249
00:11:47,679 --> 00:11:48,639
Here, take it along.

250
00:11:50,159 --> 00:11:50,539
Chinese bacon.

251
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:51,519
Right, Mom.

252
00:11:52,519 --> 00:11:54,139
This Chinese bacon, take it along.

253
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:56,639
This was saved specially for old Qian.

254
00:11:57,399 --> 00:11:58,539
I'm not even living with him anymore.

255
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:00,500
So who cares about Chinese bacon?

256
00:12:00,639 --> 00:12:01,960
So you're really getting divorced?

257
00:12:04,419 --> 00:12:05,080
It's my dad.

258
00:12:09,299 --> 00:12:09,740
Mom.

259
00:12:10,899 --> 00:12:11,460
He's here.

260
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:12,759
Sis.

261
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,159
Come in and sit, come in and sit.

262
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:14,460
Yes.

263
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:15,200
Don't just stand in the doorway.

264
00:12:15,259 --> 00:12:15,720
Fanzhu.

265
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:16,440
Come.

266
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:20,639
Take it all.

267
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:21,259
Meimei.

268
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,759
I just want to say a few words to you.

269
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:26,100
Then I'll leave.

270
00:12:28,799 --> 00:12:30,159
You've got some nerve showing up here.

271
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:44,100
Grandma, I want Chinese bacon too!

272
00:12:50,259 --> 00:12:51,320
Eight years of marriage,

273
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,179
a seven-year-old kid,

274
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:55,639
and a secret stash of 100,000.

275
00:12:57,019 --> 00:12:57,440
Tell me.

276
00:12:58,019 --> 00:12:59,460
What else don't I know about?

277
00:13:00,139 --> 00:13:01,539
It's really not a secret stash.

278
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,539
I saved it as a lifeline for you.

279
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:08,820
In case something happens to me,

280
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:10,220
you'd still have a way out.

281
00:13:11,159 --> 00:13:11,700
A way out?

282
00:13:11,919 --> 00:13:13,120
Where could I possibly go?

283
00:13:14,539 --> 00:13:15,139
Qian Dewang,

284
00:13:16,279 --> 00:13:18,440
you've already driven me to a dead end.

285
00:13:19,279 --> 00:13:20,740
Don't push me into dragging each other

286
00:13:20,759 --> 00:13:21,399
through the mud.

287
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:22,480
Stop with the crazy metaphors.

288
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,379
I'm just afraid that one day the two of us

289
00:13:24,379 --> 00:13:25,360
won't be able to make it work,

290
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,940
so at least you'd have an emergency fund.

291
00:13:28,259 --> 00:13:29,539
Open a little shop in the county town,

292
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:30,720
raise Dandan up,

293
00:13:31,139 --> 00:13:32,299
and you and the kid would want for nothing.

294
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,200
Then I could rest easy.

295
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:35,159
Open a shop for me in the county town?

296
00:13:35,399 --> 00:13:36,679
If you're so capable, open one for me

297
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,580
in Shenzhen instead!

298
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:38,080
Look at you.

299
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:38,799
Here you go again.

300
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:39,519
You just want to dump

301
00:13:39,539 --> 00:13:40,320
me and the kid.

302
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:40,779
No, I don't.

303
00:13:41,299 --> 00:13:41,799
I don't.

304
00:13:41,799 --> 00:13:43,080
You heartless jerk!

305
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:45,460
You heartless jerk, you!

306
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:45,840
Just listen to me.

307
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:46,639
If you come back with me,

308
00:13:46,639 --> 00:13:47,840
it's all debt collectors over there.

309
00:13:48,659 --> 00:13:49,740
You couldn't even sleep in peace.

310
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:50,679
Wouldn't that be a living hell?

311
00:13:52,379 --> 00:13:53,039
A living hell?

312
00:13:53,379 --> 00:13:54,379
Like I've suffered any less!

313
00:13:54,779 --> 00:13:55,860
Have I suffered any less?

314
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,379
I called you and you didn't pick up,

315
00:13:57,419 --> 00:13:58,200
you never called back either.

316
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,059
Meimei.

317
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:05,700
You...

318
00:14:07,460 --> 00:14:08,360
Just listen to me.

319
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:09,100
I...

320
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:13,460
I...

321
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:20,620
My cab is rushing me.

322
00:14:20,820 --> 00:14:21,679
I really have to go.

323
00:14:22,659 --> 00:14:23,779
All the money is right here.

324
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:25,480
The PIN is your birthday.

325
00:14:50,399 --> 00:14:50,940
Dewang

326
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:53,919
Dewang

327
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:55,240
Mom

328
00:14:55,259 --> 00:14:55,500
Here

329
00:14:55,879 --> 00:14:56,399
Dewang

330
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:58,440
This is your favorite. Take it.

331
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:00,759
Mom

332
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:01,980
You always think of me

333
00:15:02,879 --> 00:15:03,799
Every year, what I miss most

334
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:04,840
is this taste of yours

335
00:15:06,279 --> 00:15:06,639
Mom

336
00:15:07,559 --> 00:15:08,360
Take good care of yourself

337
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:09,600
Oh, right

338
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,059
Say hi to my big brother for me

339
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:12,899
Your brother's off filling up

340
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:13,799
Fanyan's car with gas

341
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:14,960
He'll be back soon

342
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,200
Just wait a little longer

343
00:15:16,679 --> 00:15:17,639
The car I called is already here

344
00:15:18,379 --> 00:15:19,100
Qian Dewang

345
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:21,519
You can't just divorce

346
00:15:21,539 --> 00:15:22,600
whenever you feel like it

347
00:15:23,039 --> 00:15:23,360
Mom

348
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:24,659
I'm heading off now

349
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:28,500
Slow down, slow down, Dandan

350
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,019
Dandan, slow down

351
00:15:31,980 --> 00:15:33,159
Let's talk this out

352
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:34,419
Dad

353
00:15:34,899 --> 00:15:36,259
My mom doesn't want to divorce you

354
00:15:36,279 --> 00:15:37,620
How come you can't see that?

355
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:38,919
Even I can tell

356
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:40,019
Who says we're not divorcing?

357
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:42,940
Driver

358
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,519
Back to Shenzhen right now

359
00:15:47,159 --> 00:15:47,779
Divorce

360
00:15:50,159 --> 00:15:51,059
I'm getting this divorce, no matter what

361
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:51,700
Enough

362
00:15:54,259 --> 00:15:55,159
Let's talk it out

363
00:16:04,379 --> 00:16:05,440
Dandan, your homework

364
00:16:06,039 --> 00:16:06,940
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

365
00:16:07,639 --> 00:16:08,580
I'll mail it back to you

366
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:13,299
Mom

367
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:15,580
Do you think those two will really divorce?

368
00:16:16,899 --> 00:16:17,500
No way

369
00:16:18,659 --> 00:16:19,679
I doubt it

370
00:16:20,179 --> 00:16:21,440
My second sister's such a money-grubber

371
00:16:21,519 --> 00:16:22,799
and my brother-in-law owes so much debt

372
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,740
Well, just you wait and see

373
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:26,120
Grandma

374
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:26,960
Uncle

375
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:27,720
Where's my mom?

376
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:28,500
She hasn't left yet, has she?

377
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:29,700
She's still home

378
00:16:30,019 --> 00:16:30,539
Great

379
00:16:42,779 --> 00:16:43,120
Yan'er

380
00:16:43,519 --> 00:16:44,759
I've packed all my stuff

381
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:46,360
When are you coming to pick me up?

382
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:53,720
What are you doing here?

383
00:16:55,519 --> 00:16:56,340
Where's your fiancé?

384
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:57,820
Doesn't even bother

385
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:58,659
to help carry your luggage.

386
00:16:58,679 --> 00:16:59,299
What's going on?

387
00:17:00,799 --> 00:17:01,379
I was actually

388
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:03,759
about to go find you

389
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:08,079
Ever since you were little

390
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:09,859
every year I put money

391
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,359
into this card for you

392
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,640
I didn't give it to you before

393
00:17:14,279 --> 00:17:15,440
because I thought you weren't grown up yet

394
00:17:16,460 --> 00:17:17,319
afraid you'd waste it

395
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:20,559
Now you're all grown up

396
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:21,680
so take it

397
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:25,160
I don't want it

398
00:17:27,339 --> 00:17:28,220
You've already paid

399
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:29,140
Granny's medical bills

400
00:17:29,579 --> 00:17:30,440
I don't need money anymore

401
00:17:31,619 --> 00:17:32,279
Besides

402
00:17:32,940 --> 00:17:34,720
I still haven't paid back what I owe you

403
00:17:35,519 --> 00:17:36,440
I don't want to owe you any more

404
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:40,000
When I say take it, just take it

405
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,299
Consider it me buying in as a partner

406
00:17:44,099 --> 00:17:45,119
Just don't lose it all

407
00:17:47,859 --> 00:17:48,920
I wonder

408
00:17:49,339 --> 00:17:50,700
who was it that said before

409
00:17:51,859 --> 00:17:53,599
that nail art is the most boring thing

410
00:17:53,619 --> 00:17:55,119
in the whole world

411
00:17:55,279 --> 00:17:56,200
I still think

412
00:17:56,279 --> 00:17:57,339
nail art is all flashy nonsense

413
00:17:57,339 --> 00:17:58,119
completely useless

414
00:17:58,900 --> 00:17:59,720
But you like it

415
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:01,420
so what can I do about it?

416
00:18:02,099 --> 00:18:02,539
I'm off now

417
00:18:03,859 --> 00:18:04,799
You're about to leave

418
00:18:05,099 --> 00:18:06,019
and you won't even let me meet

419
00:18:06,019 --> 00:18:06,900
your fiancé

420
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:08,839
Your taste was never great to begin with

421
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,119
You're about to get engaged

422
00:18:10,119 --> 00:18:11,480
and you won't let anyone check him out for you

423
00:18:15,339 --> 00:18:16,380
Even if you're engaged

424
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:18,259
you can't spend all day revolving around a man

425
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:19,559
You need a life of your own

426
00:18:19,599 --> 00:18:20,720
Figure out your own direction

427
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:21,339
Did you hear me?

428
00:18:22,819 --> 00:18:23,619
Listening to you talk

429
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:25,759
you sound like you've been there

430
00:18:28,059 --> 00:18:29,200
I mean, this time you came back

431
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:31,299
and never once mentioned Dou Cheng

432
00:18:32,119 --> 00:18:33,119
You don't even wear your engagement ring

433
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:34,799
Putting on a brave face in front of family

434
00:18:34,799 --> 00:18:36,240
and putting on a brave face in front of me too

435
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,299
Aren't you exhausted?

436
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,720
Why is it that you too

437
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,079
spend all day worrying about others?

438
00:18:42,039 --> 00:18:43,880
Couldn't you inherit some of my good traits?

439
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:46,200
I did inherit them

440
00:18:47,099 --> 00:18:48,099
Worrying about you, that's how

441
00:19:02,619 --> 00:19:03,160
I don't even know

442
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,099
when it was exactly

443
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:05,619
that I ended up like this

444
00:19:06,839 --> 00:19:07,920
I remember as a kid

445
00:19:08,299 --> 00:19:10,240
for twenty cents of malt candy

446
00:19:10,759 --> 00:19:11,579
I'd skip class

447
00:19:12,259 --> 00:19:13,460
I'd go out and get into fights

448
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:18,680
Now

449
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:20,319
there's no more twenty-cent

450
00:19:20,339 --> 00:19:21,079
malt candy anymore

451
00:19:22,779 --> 00:19:23,119
And me,

452
00:19:24,099 --> 00:19:25,819
I can't go back to those days either

453
00:19:28,299 --> 00:19:28,900
Hold on

454
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:06,900
Mom

455
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:09,440
Two cents

456
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,099
So sweet

457
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:22,180
Same taste as always

458
00:21:26,579 --> 00:21:27,180
No more crying

459
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:31,319
Here, have another one

460
00:21:52,619 --> 00:21:53,140
Mom

461
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:55,759
Jingjing

462
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,019
Mom

463
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:03,599
I love you

464
00:22:09,299 --> 00:22:10,140
I love you more

465
00:22:41,380 --> 00:22:43,119
They all just up and left.

466
00:22:44,380 --> 00:22:45,740
Who knows when

467
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,359
they'll come back again.

468
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:49,779
Before long,

469
00:22:50,380 --> 00:22:51,279
it'll be New Year's.

470
00:22:52,099 --> 00:22:53,400
These past two months, we've gone through

471
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,519
quite a few sacks of rice at home.

472
00:22:58,079 --> 00:22:58,720
My aunts

473
00:22:58,720 --> 00:22:59,740
stayed all this time

474
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:00,839
because they were worried about me.

475
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:04,859
But you, though,

476
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:07,920
it can't have been for my sake.

477
00:23:09,779 --> 00:23:10,240
Me?

478
00:23:12,039 --> 00:23:13,640
Why wouldn't I be worried about you?

479
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:15,299
Yang Xiaofang,

480
00:23:19,660 --> 00:23:20,799
my first marriage

481
00:23:20,799 --> 00:23:21,660
was held at your place.

482
00:23:22,059 --> 00:23:22,759
So for this second marriage,

483
00:23:22,759 --> 00:23:23,579
can I get a discount?

484
00:23:24,460 --> 00:23:24,940
Sure, sure, sure.

485
00:23:25,099 --> 00:23:25,940
As long as there's a discount,

486
00:23:26,039 --> 00:23:26,940
we'll hold it at your place again.

487
00:23:27,460 --> 00:23:27,900
Great, great, great.

488
00:23:28,799 --> 00:23:29,119
Yan'er.

489
00:23:33,519 --> 00:23:34,059
Look at that,

490
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,099
it's stuck.

491
00:23:36,819 --> 00:23:37,619
What a coincidence.

492
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:41,000
Good news puts a spring in your step!

493
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:41,859
Yan'er,

494
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:42,920
look how great you look

495
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,359
in the clothes I bought you.

496
00:23:45,019 --> 00:23:46,200
You used to say you didn't like them,

497
00:23:46,539 --> 00:23:47,460
that they looked dowdy.

498
00:23:48,940 --> 00:23:50,200
This is such wonderful news.

499
00:23:51,119 --> 00:23:51,759
Let's hurry along.

500
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:52,960
Let me tell you,

501
00:23:53,420 --> 00:23:55,039
I've got the banquet all arranged.

502
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:57,579
This time you won't need to worry about a thing.

503
00:23:57,859 --> 00:23:59,299
Just relax and be the bride.

504
00:23:59,539 --> 00:24:00,279
So soon?

505
00:24:02,420 --> 00:24:03,740
Is it that same hotel

506
00:24:03,740 --> 00:24:04,799
from your first wedding?

507
00:24:05,660 --> 00:24:07,519
For a repeat customer on a second marriage,

508
00:24:07,759 --> 00:24:09,240
did they give you a big discount,

509
00:24:09,319 --> 00:24:10,279
throw in a lot of dishes,

510
00:24:10,599 --> 00:24:11,660
and a lot of drinks too?

511
00:24:12,740 --> 00:24:13,059
Well,

512
00:24:15,099 --> 00:24:16,500
save where you can, spend where you should.

513
00:24:18,019 --> 00:24:18,680
As for the ring,

514
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:19,660
I didn't skimp on it one bit.

515
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:21,980
What lands in your own pocket

516
00:24:22,119 --> 00:24:23,099
is called living.

517
00:24:23,460 --> 00:24:25,599
What goes to someone else is called waste.

518
00:24:26,279 --> 00:24:26,740
Come here.

519
00:24:27,220 --> 00:24:28,279
I've got a gift for you too.

520
00:24:36,779 --> 00:24:37,539
Give me your hand.

521
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:40,160
Close your eyes.

522
00:24:41,039 --> 00:24:41,799
There's a little surprise.

523
00:24:44,799 --> 00:24:45,619
Ow, ow, ow, that hurts!

524
00:24:46,660 --> 00:24:47,619
This ring you bought is too small,

525
00:24:47,619 --> 00:24:48,140
it doesn't fit.

526
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:49,180
Can it be returned?

527
00:24:49,220 --> 00:24:50,380
Of course it can be returned.

528
00:24:50,980 --> 00:24:52,200
Not just the ring's going back,

529
00:24:52,740 --> 00:24:53,619
the man's going back too.

530
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:00,440
Isn't this the big diamond ring

531
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:01,079
I bought for you?

532
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:02,039
Yes, it is.

533
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:03,720
Fan Yan, what's that supposed to mean?

534
00:25:04,720 --> 00:25:05,720
What I mean is,

535
00:25:05,859 --> 00:25:06,839
return this ring

536
00:25:07,299 --> 00:25:08,779
and hire yourself a better nanny.

537
00:25:09,319 --> 00:25:10,220
Because I,

538
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:12,980
I'm done waiting on you!

539
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:32,700
Wait, hold on

540
00:25:33,500 --> 00:25:34,519
Yang Fanyan, where are you going?

541
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:38,839
The Maldives

542
00:27:28,599 --> 00:27:29,180
Hurry up and write it

543
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:31,380
I've got things to do once you're done

544
00:27:32,859 --> 00:27:33,980
This is all I'm capable of

545
00:27:35,099 --> 00:27:36,000
I'm the one who let you down

546
00:27:36,980 --> 00:27:37,660
Don't hesitate anymore

547
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:09,319
I... I'm not getting divorced.

548
00:28:09,319 --> 00:28:09,839
I'm not divorcing you.

549
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:11,880
Meimei.

550
00:28:12,759 --> 00:28:13,140
What is it?

551
00:28:13,819 --> 00:28:15,200
I'm not getting divorced.

552
00:28:19,099 --> 00:28:19,759
Give... give it to me.

553
00:28:22,660 --> 00:28:23,440
Just wait a second.

554
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:30,680
Why are you backing out now?

555
00:28:32,019 --> 00:28:33,059
It's 800,000 yuan!

556
00:28:33,819 --> 00:28:35,079
So what, we just pay it back.

557
00:28:35,500 --> 00:28:36,420
We'll pay it off.

558
00:28:41,039 --> 00:28:41,619
Meimei.

559
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:43,319
I was wrong.

560
00:28:43,700 --> 00:28:44,500
I really was wrong.

561
00:28:45,299 --> 00:28:45,640
I...

562
00:28:46,980 --> 00:28:48,019
"I" what?

563
00:28:49,380 --> 00:28:50,500
It's just a few hundred grand.

564
00:28:51,240 --> 00:28:51,880
I, Yang Fanmei,

565
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:53,039
can endure any hardship there is.

566
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:56,339
I owe more than just that.

567
00:29:01,759 --> 00:29:02,420
How much do you owe?

568
00:29:02,980 --> 00:29:03,460
900,000.

569
00:29:04,160 --> 00:29:04,740
How much exactly?

570
00:29:05,819 --> 00:29:06,460
One million.

571
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:07,819
How did it jump to a million?

572
00:29:07,819 --> 00:29:08,900
How much exactly?

573
00:29:09,480 --> 00:29:10,519
1.1 million.

574
00:29:11,259 --> 00:29:12,299
Really, that's all of it.

575
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:15,140
Tell me the truth.

576
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:16,779
You, Qian Dewang...

577
00:29:20,660 --> 00:29:21,259
Officer.

578
00:29:22,920 --> 00:29:23,440
Stamp it.

579
00:29:26,259 --> 00:29:26,859
Officer.

580
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:29,240
